From: Nfrastack <code@nfrastack.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: left panel collapses on fullscreen transition

Bug: When transitioning from maximized to fullscreen in Hyprland (or any
WM where the window briefly reports a smaller size during the transition),
react-resizable-panels sees available space drop below minSize and
auto-collapses the panel because the `collapsible` prop is set.

The viewmodel (ResizerViewModel) still manages collapse/expand via
separator click and double-click — removing `collapsible` from the
Panel props just prevents auto-collapse on transient resize events.

Upstream issue: When window transitions from maximized to fullscreen,
the container briefly shrinks -> react-resizable-panels auto-collapses
the left panel because collapsible=true.

diff --git a/packages/shared-components/src/resize/panel/LeftResizablePanelView.tsx b/packages/shared-components/src/resize/panel/LeftResizablePanelView.tsx
index 9b3ac2fe7e..4fdfb4c164 100644
--- a/packages/shared-components/src/resize/panel/LeftResizablePanelView.tsx
+++ b/packages/shared-components/src/resize/panel/LeftResizablePanelView.tsx
@@ -60,7 +60,6 @@ export function LeftResizablePanelView({
             inert={isCollapsed}
             id={LEFT_PANEL_ID}
             className={className}
-            collapsible
             minSize={props.minSize}
             maxSize={props.maxSize}
             defaultSize={defaultSize}
